# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# jeffs_math_explainer_videos
#
# Sources, scripts, facts, oracles, lexicons, storyboards and research live in
# git. Everything an explainer *generates* (video, audio, frames, sheets,
# narration takes, ASR databases, build trees) is regenerable and stays out:
# a single 4K master is ~200 MB, over GitHub's 100 MB file limit. Finished
# cuts ship as GitHub Release assets instead (see README "Releases").
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Rust build output -------------------------------------------------------
/target/
target/
target-*/
target_*/
.rch-target/
.rch-target-*/
.rch-results/

# --- Rendered media: never commit -------------------------------------------
*.mp4
*.mov
*.mkv
*.webm
*.gif
*.y4m
*.m4a
*.aac
*.flac
*.mp3
*.ogg
*.wav
*.partial.wav
**/renders/
**/draft/
**/draft_*/
**/out/
**/frames/
**/glyphs_probe/
**/previous/
concat.txt

# Contact sheets, cue sheets and other review PNGs are build products.
# Hand-picked README stills live under docs/media/ and are allowed.
*.png
!**/docs/media/*.png
!docs/media/**/*.png

# --- Narration pipeline work dirs (regenerable with ./x narrate) ------------
**/narration/
**/narration_work/
**/narration_takes/
**/probes_work/
# Text records of a *shipped* narration (spoken.tsv, review.tsv, report.json)
# are kept deliberately; see explainer_corpus/hoeffding_d/narration_v5/.

# --- Music / score stems (regenerable from the score DSL) -------------------
# stems_<cut>/ are an earlier cut's stems, set aside beside the ones replacing them.
**/stems/
**/stems_*/
**/score_cache/

# --- franken_whisper QA state (SQLite DB, WAL, temp audio) ------------------
.franken_whisper/
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-*

# --- ./x driver gate markers and logs (per machine) ------------------------
**/.x/
**/logs/
*.log
logs_render_all.txt
nohup.out

# --- Per-machine settings ---------------------------------------------------
project.env
**/project.env
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!project.env.example
.claude/settings.local.json
# private machine/account names for tools/scan_private.sh (naming them here would publish them)
.private_patterns

# --- Profiling captures -----------------------------------------------------
# macOS `sample` output embeds the host's process list and local paths.
**/perf/mac/
**/perf/**/sample_*.txt
*.trace
flamegraph*.svg
perf.data
perf.data.old

# --- franken_manim caches & provenance sidecars ----------------------------
.fmn-cache/
*.fmncache
*.provenance.json
*.repro-bundle
*.replay
*.journal

